meta {
  name: 17-Try to check verification status
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/api/verifications/mine
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{temi_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: in [200, 401, 404]
}

docs {
  After submitting, I want to know "is my NIN being reviewed?". I
  expect a `GET /verifications/mine` or some endpoint that shows me
  PENDING / APPROVED / REJECTED for my submission.

  But the OpenAPI spec ONLY exposes:
  - POST /verifications (submit)
  - GET /admin/verifications (admin queue)
  - POST /admin/verifications/{id}/approve|reject (admin decisions)

  There is no read-side for the submitter. Me, as Temi, cannot
  check the status of my own verification. I just have to wait
  blindly until a notification fires. That is a finding.

  Trying the URL anyway — expecting 404.
}
